2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A branch of this German noble family moved to Poland and became Polonized over centuries.
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT https://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unruh
2 CONT
2 CONT Perennial nobility of German origin probably originating from Franconia. The first members of this family were: Ernestus Unrowe, mentioned in 1212, and Conradus Unrowe, mentioned in 1233. Genealogical line of the family from Jan U
2 CONC nruwe, mentioned in 1310 near the Silesian Brzeg . Largely reproduced, divided into many lines, branches and houses, several of which settled in Wielkopolska underwent permanent Polonization from the 17th century with a change of 
2 CONC name to "Unrug". The ancestor of the baronial branch known as Wendstadt Linden was Hans Siegmund (1644–1694). His son Johann Wilhelm von Unruh (1668–1728) owned the estateWągroda (Wendstadt, Kreis Guhrau) in the Górowo poviat . He
2 CONC  received the Czech elevation to the old state of lords with the confirmation of the family coat of arms by the imperial office in Vienna on January 14, 1719. His descendants settled in the vicinity of Góra , moved to Greater Pola
2 CONC nd at the beginning of the 19th century and through marriages underwent permanent Polonization.
