1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Perleberger Stadtfeld, and the Stadtforst, as well as a tower (the so-called "Burgfriede"), which Liudke von Quitzow bought from the city council in 1556. Ludke was married to Anna von Oberg (died 1591), who had br
2 CONC ought a considerable wealth into the marriage. According to an old sandstone plaque on the tower of the castle, dated 1546, it must be assumed that this property was applied to a hereditary fief with the conversion of the Pfandbes
2 CONC itzes Stavenow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jahrbuch für brandenburgische Landesgeschichte, Volume 51 [snippet]
