1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Friedrich Wilhelm von Kickstedt, II''' was born circa 1675. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich Wilhelm married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34727928113 Helene Juliane von Peterswald]. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34727928200 Wilhelm von Peters-wald]. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT The Peterswalds were originally a noble family of Silesia, where they resided at the castle of Peterswaldau, in the district of Reichenbach, governed by Arnold von Peters- wald in 1322. The family, which was very wealthy in the fi
2 CONC rst half of the seventeenth century, had come into Franken, Southern Germany, and had been admitted in the knights canton of Rhon Werra. Branches of the family went subsequently to Sweden, Hanover, &c. Carl Friedrich von Peters- w
2 CONC ald, royal master of the horse of Great Britain and Brunswick Luneburg, &c, in 1752, son of Maximilian von Peterswald, by his wife, Elizabeth von Kussow on the Hardt, in his will, dated 1752, made his heir the eldest son of his si
2 CONC ster, '''Helene Juliane von Peterswald (who was b. 1680, and m. 1700), by her husband, Friedrich Wilhelm, II von Kickstedt''', on condition that he took the additional surname and arms of von Peters- wald. Wilhelm von Peterswald l
2 CONC eft Germany for political reasons about the year 1770, and settled in Exeter, co. Devon, where he and had two sons, William and John, who emigrated to Jamaica, West Indies, where they possessed an estate named Petersfield, St. Mar
2 CONC y, and were successful as planters. The latter, John, d. s.p. 20th November, 1814, at Jamaica, aged 38 years, and the former, William Peterswald, Esq., sometime colonel of the St. Mary's 1st Regiment (West Indies), m. at Kingston,
2 CONC  Jamaica, 23rd June, 1823, Jean, daughter of Captain Walter Gray, of the Sutherland Fenciblrs, by Eliza, his wife, daughter of Sir Arthur Nicolson, of Lochend, Shetland, Bart., and d. at Liverpool, 25th August, 1818, aged 72, leav
2 CONC ing by her (who was b. 6th November, 1790, and d. at Adelaide, 1868, aged 78) an only child, the present William John Peterswald, Esq.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms—Or. on a fesse sa. a boar's head fessewise erased pointing towards the sinister. Crest—Out of a ducal coronet two elephants' trunks erect.
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence: Residence —St. Ileliers, Adelaide, South Australia.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ia601408.us.archive.org/34/items/genealogicalhera01burk/genealogicalhera01burk.pdf
